From: Gran Turismo 6 for Mac <https://github.com/Wooloomooloo2/Gran-Turismo-6-Mac>
Subject: [PATCH] lv2 page-fault notification (327, 57) and real memory objects

Upstream: not yet submitted; written to be upstreamed (generic, no title names)
Licence: MIT, as ps3recomp (see its LICENSE); offered under the same terms
Base: ps3recomp 4e8f3ca87a3e1d87bb83b8b7e9348fe2685cd514 (after 0001-0028)

What: sys_mmapper_enable_page_fault_notification (lv2 327) was an
unimplemented syscall that answered CELL_OK, and sys_mmapper_map_memory /
unmap_memory / free_memory answered CELL_OK and did nothing. Now:
- 327 registers a page-fault queue for a reserved area (EINVAL unless the
  address is the area's start, ESRCH for an unknown queue, EBUSY for a
  second registration, as RPCS3 models lv2). The area's pages with no memory
  object mapped become inaccessible on the host.
- A guest PPU thread that touches such a page is suspended in the fault
  handler and lv2's event goes to the queue: source
  SYS_MEMORY_PAGE_FAULT_EVENT_KEY, data1 the address, data2
  (SYS_MEMORY_PAGE_FAULT_TYPE_PPU_THREAD << 32) | thread id, data3
  SYS_MEMORY_PAGE_FAULT_CAUSE_NON_MAPPED. sys_ppu_thread_recover_page_fault
  (lv2 57) resumes it and the access re-runs (EINVAL for a thread that is not
  suspended). sys_spu_thread_recover_page_fault (lv2 198) is EINVAL: SPU
  faults are not delivered (below).
- Memory objects (runtime/syscalls/sys_mmapper_pf.c) keep their contents
  while unmapped: in a page-fault area unmap copies the object out and map
  copies it back. unmap answers the object's id (EINVAL with nothing mapped
  there), map is ESRCH / EALIGN / EBUSY as lv2, free is EBUSY while mapped.
  Outside page-fault areas the flat VM is unchanged.
Not covered: an SPU or host (RSX, audio) thread touching an unmapped page is
not suspended; the page is committed empty and reported on stderr.

Why: a title's pager reserves an area, enables notification and maps file
contents in only when a thread faults on a page. Nothing ever faulted, so
the area read as zeros: a database file paged in that way read as an empty
file, SQLite answered SQLITE_NOTADB to every query on it, and the title's
script failed on the missing rows and restarted its whole start-up.

Test: tools/test_mmapper_page_fault.py (new) builds
tests/test_mmapper_page_fault.c with the real sys_event.c, sys_memory.c and
sys_mmapper_pf.c: 327's error answers, a thread faulting on an unmapped page,
the event's four words, the pager's map and 57, the thread seeing the
pager's data, unmap's id, contents kept across unmap and map, and the map,
unmap and free errors.

